*.mp4
furlpay*.png
wear os*.png

# Lead/prospect data. Contains contact details for real individuals and this
# repo has outside collaborators. Keep it out of version control entirely.
furlpay_prospects_enriched_v2.csv
furlpay_prospects_enriched_v2.xlsx

# Scratch capture of a third-party site, kept locally for analysis only. It
# contains another company's minified bundle and branding, so it must never
# enter this repo's history — committing it would ship their code inside a
# commercial product.
furlpay_pay/

# Cloned capture of tangem.com, kept locally as a design/reference artefact.
# Same reasoning as furlpay_pay/ above: it is another company's markup, minified
# bundles, fonts and branding. It must never enter this repo's history.
reference/

# Product screenshots kept locally for design review. Same reasoning as the
# marketing assets above: multi-MB PNGs are permanent once committed. The
# existing furlpay*.png / wear os*.png rules did not cover these filenames.
/hotels map.png
/portfolio dashboard.png
/portfolio dashboard and wallet.png
/screen app 2 .png
/ticket confirmation screen.png
/trading chart.png

# Scratch scaffolding that rewrites audit/mobile-ux-audit.md from empty.
# Keeping it in the repo invites someone to run it and truncate the audit.
/build_sections.py

# Another company's logo, kept locally as a reference artefact only.
/wikiexpo-lo.svg

# Personal fundraising / founder-community research. Not product material and
# this repo has outside collaborators.
/fintech_founder_opportunities_2026.csv
/stablecoin_funding_investors_2026.csv
